# BUGS

An eMMC runs at high speed at most: no HS200 or HS400, nor its boot and RPMB partitions, and the K1's 8-bit bus is used only where its capabilities say it has one.
An eMMC has been brought up only in QEMU: the Orange Pi RV2 has no eMMC module fitted.
UHS is off: on the Orange Pi RV2 a card (a 32 GB `LX32G`) takes CMD11 and holds CMD and DAT[3:0] low, and still holds them 100 ms after the clock comes back at 1.8 V, though with the card idle the pads read the lines high at 1.8 V; a card left so answers nothing, and the slot's disk is gone, until the board loses power. SDR50, SDR104 and the tuning have never run on hardware.
No DDR50, and no card's current limit or driver strength is set (CMD6's groups 3 and 4): a card runs SDR104 at its default 200 mA.
The tuning isn't repeated: a card that drifts from its delay fails requests until the driver starts again.
The card's supply, the PMIC's buck4, is always on, so a card at 1.8 V stays there until the board is powered off: a warm boot finds it so, and after a reset the firmware talks to it at 3.3 V, as it does after Linux.
There is no card detect and no removal: a card is looked for once, when the driver starts, and taking it out fails the requests that follow.
Only one card a slot, one request at a time, and the data is copied between the client's ring and the driver's memory.
